                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]A Brain Training Adventure Game[/h1]\nhttps://youtu.be/0WegLX7EugA\n+ The gameplay is very enjoyable. Basically you watch animated cutscenes while doing quick time events, and a math problem during each scene. \n+ Very amusing characters. The main character \"Chilie\" is a young girl who loves peppers, and makes all sorts of crazy noises and faces with her guardian as she searches for her mother.\n+ Very sppealing unique visual style \n+ The math puzzles can be quite challenging at times. Basically you have to reach a number in a certain number of actions using addition / subtraction / multiplication / division but have a limited number of choices. Hard to explain in writing, but later on in the game these puzzles will make you think.\n\n- Throughout each scene there are various numbers you can click on which will help make the math puzzles a bit easier. The numbers you find are random each time you play a scene, so sometimes you find numbers that will make the puzzle super easy, while other times it feels seemingly impossible. ( You can skip the puzzles, but I felt like I needed to solve them )",
